/*
===============================================================================
DDL Script: Create and Clean Bronze Tables (Manual Import Workflow)
===============================================================================
Script Purpose:
    This script defines the 'Bronze Layer' (Raw Data) structure for MySQL.
    Because the Table Data Import Wizard is used instead of 'LOAD DATA', 
    we use a 'VARCHAR Staging Strategy'.

Workflow:
	0. Use Terminal open MySQLWorkbench "open /Applications/MySQLWorkbench.app"
    Reference: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nXqwDcRF304
    1. CREATE: Define all tables with VARCHAR columns to prevent import crashes.
    2. IMPORT: Right-click table -> Table Data Import Wizard -> Select CSV.
    3. CLEAN: Run the UPDATE NULLIF statements to turn empty strings ('') and spaces (' ') into NULLs.
    4. TRANSFORM: Use UPDATE STR_TO_DATE to fix slashes (/) to dashes (-).
    5. ALTER: Modify columns to final data types (INT, DATE, DECIMAL).
===============================================================================
*/


